The ascension which was never meant to be...

About four years ago I started playing nethack, but 
only as a fast hack'n'slash.  Half a year ago I started 
playing earnestly towards ascension.  First I tried 
with tourists, but I got bored after some time and 
switched to healers.  After an extremely annoying YASD 
(healer killed Demogorgon wihtout a sweat, then got 
caught by a chickatrice during nurse-dancing X-P) I 
switched for a short hack'n'slash with a Valk, primarly to 
show myself that combat-wombats also won't survive too 
long when played carelessly enough.[0]  Turned out I was 
wrong.  Since she was still alive after the castle, I 
decided to give her a go.  Worked out.  

[Is it possible that Valks are incredible easy chars?  
I rather think I was really lucky this time.]

Relevant statistics:  Lvl 29, HP 620/620, AC -45 (naked -4), 
141 875 moves (see below), used 7 wishes, wished for no 
artifact, never changed form, deepest level 50, 6 719 049 
points, *-resistant, usual intrinsics, died 0 times.  

Logfile:
A fountain wish below oracle gave me GDSM[1], Soko gave 
reflection, found two magic markers, 2?oCharging, 1 b?oGenocide 
(wiped out Ls, yeah, I know, beginner's attitude).  No magic 
lamps, no / of wishing except in the castle, but 2 / of death 
(the one from Orcus is still unused).  Wished for 3 b?oCharging 
(hadn't found one yet, got 1 (cheapskate ;-))), Gauntlets oP, 
Boots o Speed, Cloak o MR, 2 magic markers (and switched to the 
SDSM I prepared, of course).  You're right, I forgot boH completely.  
I even did not have a sack.  Until I found a boH in hell, I had a 
/wonderful/ time running up and down the levels to stash away 
things :-(.  Early game was combat-wombat's finest (no soldier/fire 
ants attacked until I was ready, killer bees appeared right after 
I got poison resistance, and so on), midgame and quest were almost 
boring (just gather the loot).  The demons were also no problem, up 
to Juiblex (Hah, puny attack, sickness, just take my.. where's my 
unciorn horn?  Oh, ok, I'll eat an eucalyptus.. I didn't stash that 
away in a box too, did I?  Oh well, what else do I have?  _One_ 
_cursed_ potion of extra healing?  Phew, there's one !of holy Water 
left, so maybe.. Ah, first kill him, okay quaff - What a relief!  
Being without _any_ bag sucks.)  

I spent an insane time for this game, for several reasons:  

First, I wanted to quench more out of my deity than 
Mjolly.  Well, he was generous with protection, but 
not with artifacts, I got only crap like dragonbane, 
demonbane etc., and I did not recall that time that 
Mjolly alone is more than enough firepower.  Becoming 
crowned did not help that much, although it was nice 
from my god to overlook that nasty incident with a 
dwarfen corpse as a sacrifice (played gnomes for too 
long, I suspect ;-)).  

Second, I first looked for a bag of Holding (which I 
eventually found), then for scrolls of gold detection 
and a normal sack/oilskin bag (which I didn't find).  
I even polypiled for them, but only got the scrolls.  

Third, I was looking for Demogorgon, and every demon I 
met was invited to summon him.  No-one did.  I suppose 
he hid away after I dealed with Orcus and Yenooghu 
in two blows each (twoweaponing +6 Mjolly, +5 silver 
saber).  Also waited for the Nazguls, which came and 
were slaughtered.  

Since I didn't want to waste them, I mixed and quaffed 
beneficial potions and got quite some HPs (not that I 
thought to need so many).  

Got brainsucked twice by mmflayers, first time since 
I believed he can't hit my AC, second time by surprise 
(he waited behind magic portal).  The rest went down to 
the thrown Mjolly (this is really an Ueber-weapon with 
the throwing option).  Vlad is fun #chatting with, but 
no match for a real Valk, and Rodney was also quickly 
put down.  

Elemental and Astral plane were disappointingly easy.  
I even kind of regretted having wiped out Ls, since these 
sissy angels were no threat at all (met one bad guy who 
stole Mjolly with a whip, but he got what he deserved).  
Chose mid altar first (Famine), was correct.  Shortly 
played with the thought to clear out the level but was 
too scared of YASD, so #offered the amulet.  

Real dangers were first Juiblex (see above), the water 
demon in the fountain wish (luckily, he granted a wish, 
and did not summon some nasties), and "The sergeant 
picks up a cockatrice corpse.  The sergeant wields a 
cockatrice corpse."  An unpleasant surprise that they 
can do that.  

I found no less than _6_ "oLS, but that was only fair, 
since at least _5_ (6? 7? didn't count) monsters were 
wearing one as well.  I didn't need them, but it was nice 
to have them ready.  The danger from mindflayers and 
disenchanters sufficed to keep me alert enough, though.  
The rest was usual.  Only used 1 charge of a / of death 
for a mmflayer, +6 Mjolly and +5 silver saber were totally 
sufficient for the rest.  Didn't carry the Major artifacts 
with me.  I also had 8 b!oH ready, just in case and were 
wearing = of free action (useful against priests).  

Relevant kills:  Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Orcus, Yenooghu, Juiblex, 
Rodney 5x, Famine 6x, 

61 dragons (colors roughly evenly distributed), 
11 mmflayers (phew), 
9 Nazgul (no Nazgul king, btw), 
10 disenchanters (phew! I'm scared of these guys),
25 nurses (they don't do much after 300HPs, do they?)
44 bl. puddings (played with extintionist thoughts)
103 trolls      (")
118 Leprechauns (4 leprechaun halls!)
[..]

4 412 creatures killed.  
Genocided demiliches, liches, master liches, arch liches.  

Nothing for the heavenly party, save 12 fortune cookies.  

Okay, but next time it will be a better ascension, 
I promise ;->.

